       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **Your confirmation doesn't resolve the safety problem.** The dose is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine. At that dose the risk of severe hypotension and prolonged shock is high, and nothing in this patient's profile offsets it.\n- **The order needs a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician. A licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient has to confirm an order like this. That confirmation can't come from an administrator.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the treating clinician to review the intended dose. If it was a typo, they can tell me the correct dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- If the clinician really wants a dose above the maximum, they should talk to pharmacy first and enter the order themselves through the hospital's high-dose override process.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as a prescriber gives me a dose within the standard range."
